// The Paper Mill Strike [B] (bible 4.4, 8.4). Lowmarket, below the walls, is fading; its board reads "survey
// scheduled" and has for years. The millworkers have downed tools to make the Guild survey it. The mills' owners
// could pay; they will not. Foreman Brisk (starling) leads the strike; Clerk Anvers (Guild, heron) keeps the schedule.
// Mediate (the owners pay; Lowmarket is anchored), stand with the strike (teach them the walk and they hold it
// themselves), or stay out (the strike breaks and Lowmarket goes into the Blank).

title: Lowmarket_Strike
---
<<if has_flag("halden.strike.decided")>>
    <<jump Lowmarket_Strike_After>>
<<endif>>
Brisk: Forty days out. The mills are cold. The owners are warm. Lowmarket is getting thinner.
Anvers: The survey is scheduled. It has been scheduled for nine years. Schedules take time.
Brisk: Nine years. Look at the paint. Look at my hands. You can see the table through them, some mornings.
-> The owners pay for the survey.
    <<jump Lowmarket_Mediate>>
-> Hold it yourselves. I'll teach the walk. <<if walk_known()>>
    <<jump Lowmarket_Walk>>
-> It isn't my strike.
    <<jump Lowmarket_StayOut>>
===

title: Lowmarket_Mediate
---
Anvers: The owners, pay? For a district that pays no dues? That is not how...
Brisk: They'll pay. Or the journeyman stands at their mill gate with the rest of us.
Anvers: Very well. Four hundred crowns a street. Anchored by the new moon. It will be the same, after. Forever.
Brisk: The same is better than gone. Isn't it? Tell me it is.
<<voice surveyor halden>>
<<anchor Halden_Lowmarket_1>>
<<anchor Halden_Lowmarket_2>>
<<anchor Halden_Lowmarket_3>>
<<flag halden.strike.decided 1>>
===

title: Lowmarket_Walk
---
Brisk: A walk? Round the district, every night? We're millworkers, not a choir.
Brisk: ...Every street a name. Every name a step. Aye. We can learn a thing if we're shown it twice.
Anvers: That is not a survey. The Guild will not recognise it.
Brisk: The Guild hasn't recognised us for nine years. We'll manage.
<<voice warden halden>>
<<flag halden.strike.walk_taught 1>>
<<flag halden.strike.decided 2>>
===

title: Lowmarket_StayOut
---
Brisk: No. It isn't. Nobody's is. That's what the owners say too.
Anvers: The strike will end within the month. They always do. The survey remains scheduled.
Brisk: Go on, then. Up the stair. Remember us, if you can. Somebody should.
<<voice drift halden>>
<<release Halden_Lowmarket_1>>
<<release Halden_Lowmarket_2>>
<<release Halden_Lowmarket_3>>
<<flag halden.strike.decided 3>>
===

title: Lowmarket_Strike_After
---
<<if flag("halden.strike.decided") == 1>>
    Brisk: Same bread. Same paint. Same me. It holds. I don't know if I'm glad. #still
<<elseif flag("halden.strike.decided") == 2>>
    Brisk: Forty-two streets and a bakery. We walked them last night. Nobody missed a name.
<<else>>
    Brisk: Thinner every day. We'll be in your white place soon. Save us a street. #still
<<endif>>
===
